.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/fast-json-stable-stringify Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "fast-json-stable-stringify"
.PP
Deterministic \fRJSON\&.stringify()\fP - a faster version of \fR@substack\fP's json-stable-strigify without \fRjsonify\fP\&.

.PP
You can also pass in a custom comparison function\&.

.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP
.SH "example"
.PP
.PP
.nf
 js
var stringify = require('fast\-json\-stable\-stringify');
var obj = { c: 8, b: [{z:6,y:5,x:4},7], a: 3 };
console\&.log(stringify(obj));
.fi
.PP

.PP
output:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{"a":3,"b":[{"x":4,"y":5,"z":6},7],"c":8}
.fi
.PP
.SH "methods"
.PP
.PP
.nf
 js
var stringify = require('fast\-json\-stable\-stringify')
.fi
.PP
.SS "var str = stringify(obj, opts)"
Return a deterministic stringified string \fRstr\fP from the object \fRobj\fP\&.
.SS "options"
.SS "cmp"
If \fRopts\fP is given, you can supply an \fRopts\&.cmp\fP to have a custom comparison function for object keys\&. Your function \fRopts\&.cmp\fP is called with these parameters:

.PP
.PP
.nf
 js
opts\&.cmp({ key: akey, value: avalue }, { key: bkey, value: bvalue })
.fi
.PP

.PP
For example, to sort on the object key names in reverse order you could write:

.PP
.PP
.nf
 js
var stringify = require('fast\-json\-stable\-stringify');

var obj = { c: 8, b: [{z:6,y:5,x:4},7], a: 3 };
var s = stringify(obj, function (a, b) {
    return a\&.key < b\&.key ? 1 : \-1;
});
console\&.log(s);
.fi
.PP

.PP
which results in the output string:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{"c":8,"b":[{"z":6,"y":5,"x":4},7],"a":3}
.fi
.PP

.PP
Or if you wanted to sort on the object values in reverse order, you could write:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var stringify = require('fast\-json\-stable\-stringify');

var obj = { d: 6, c: 5, b: [{z:3,y:2,x:1},9], a: 10 };
var s = stringify(obj, function (a, b) {
    return a\&.value < b\&.value ? 1 : \-1;
});
console\&.log(s);
.fi
.PP

.PP
which outputs:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{"d":6,"c":5,"b":[{"z":3,"y":2,"x":1},9],"a":10}
.fi
.PP
.SS "cycles"
Pass \fRtrue\fP in \fRopts\&.cycles\fP to stringify circular property as \fR__cycle__\fP - the result will not be a valid JSON string in this case\&.

.PP
TypeError will be thrown in case of circular object without this option\&.
.SH "install"
.PP
With \fRnpm\fP do:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install fast\-json\-stable\-stringify
.fi
.PP
.SH "benchmark"
.PP
To run benchmark (requires Node\&.js 6+): 
.PP
.nf
node benchmark

.fi
.PP

.PP
Results: 
.PP
.nf
fast\-json\-stable\-stringify x 17,189 ops/sec ±1\&.43% (83 runs sampled)
json\-stable\-stringify x 13,634 ops/sec ±1\&.39% (85 runs sampled)
fast\-stable\-stringify x 20,212 ops/sec ±1\&.20% (84 runs sampled)
faster\-stable\-stringify x 15,549 ops/sec ±1\&.12% (84 runs sampled)
The fastest is fast\-stable\-stringify

.fi
.PP
